& [AuthorshipBoundary] is explicit
  + [parity_profile] is cantor-authorship-parity/0.1
  + one lane is declared hand-authored and one is declared model-shaped
  + each lane carries distinct author identity and explicit provenance evidence
  + model-shaped is a supplied provenance assertion in this fixture and not proof of a live model call
  + author identity cannot equal the lane validator, compiler, verifier, fake Observer, or coordinator
  + authorship class grants no validation, compilation, verification, admission, catalogue, invocation, truth, or effect authority

& [SamePipelineContract] is independently replayed
  + each lane receives candidate validation, a content-bound named fake validation receipt, deterministic compilation, independent static verification, exact fake Observer policy and admission, immutable catalogue insertion, two-process coordination, token cycle, and replay receipt
  + comparison independently reruns and compares every supplied stage before accepting the lane as parity evidence
  + substituted candidate, receipt, IR, procedure, policy, admission, catalogue, request, session, coordination, token, or replay evidence invalidates the lane rather than producing a parity result

& [BehaviorProjection] preserves relevant semantics
  + lane-specific candidate, compiled procedure, session, message, continuation, pass, trace-event, and receipt identities are excluded from equality where exact derivation necessarily differs by lane identity
  + normalized source, schema set, process definitions, effects, bounds, sensitivity, retention, compiler cost, pipeline principals, phase dispositions, admission contexts, revocation conditions, output, budgets, residuals, instruction sequence, trace payloads, message direction and causal shape, continuation states, token participant order, stable frame, and replay match are retained
  + exact projection equality produces passed parity
  + valid semantic or pipeline difference produces refused parity with per-axis result
  + invalid evidence produces no parity report

& [NegativeBoundary] is fail-closed
  + missing provenance, self-validation, Observer impersonation, textual source without parser authority, semantic drift, different pipeline principal, and substituted runtime evidence are distinguished
  + equal treatment is not equal merit and behavioral equality is not truth
  + no provider, model, parser, service, persistence, live transport, external process, thread, effect, hardware, or FPGA surface is present

